      "stem": "Let the foot of perpendicular from the point (λ, 2,3) on the line $\\frac{x-4}{1}=\\frac{y-9}{2}=\\frac{z-5}{1}$ be the point (1, µ, 2). Then the distance between the lines $\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y-2}{3}=\\frac{z+4}{6}$ and $\\frac{x-\\lambda}{2}=\\frac{y-\\mu}{3}=\\frac{z+5}{6}$ is equal to",
